# Environment variables
.env

# WordPress installations
#
# sites/html/ will reappear on its own (empty) the first time a phpXX
# container starts -- it's Docker auto-creating the base image's WORKDIR
# (/var/www/html, from the official wordpress:phpX-fpm image), not a real
# site. Harmless to have, but don't delete it by hand while containers are
# already running: Docker only auto-creates a missing WORKDIR when a
# container *starts*, not for `docker exec` into one already running, so
# removing it out from under a live container breaks every bare
# `docker compose exec $php_svc ...` call (no explicit --workdir) against
# it with "chdir to cwd (/var/www/html) ... no such file or directory" --
# confirmed the hard way, it silently broke wpdev status's cache check.
sites/*/

# Database data
*.sql
*.sql.gz

# Per-site snapshots (wpdev snapshot/restore) and all-DB backups (wpdev backup)
snapshots/
backups/

# Logs
logs/**/*.log

# API service (api/) — node_modules is rebuilt by the Docker image via
# package-lock.json (committed); .api-uploads is a scratch dir for
# in-flight db-import uploads, never meant to persist.
api/node_modules/
.api-uploads/

# Local SSL certs
nginx/ssl/certs/*
nginx/ssl/private/*
nginx/sites/*
!nginx/ssl/certs/.gitkeep
!nginx/ssl/private/.gitkeep
!nginx/ssl/.gitkeep
!nginx/sites/.gitkeep
!nginx/sites/default.conf
!nginx/sites/site.conf.template
!nginx/sites/site.conf.cached.template

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE files
#
# .vscode/launch.json is shipped on purpose (see README's "Xdebug" section)
# -- generic, no personal paths beyond ${workspaceFolder}, no secrets.
# Ignoring the dir outright would silently stop tracking it for anyone who
# re-generates it with a different file inside, since a `!` negation can't
# un-ignore a file inside an already-ignored directory.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/launch.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Keep directory structure
!sites/.gitkeep
!logs/.gitkeep
!nginx/ssl/.gitkeep
!nginx/ssl/certs/.gitkeep
!nginx/ssl/private/.gitkeep
